          "code": "EXPLAIN_PLAN_COMPONENT",
          "id": "1771439358431",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771439358432_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nAssume the role of someone who is a skilled Oracle Incentive Compensation plan administrator who deeply understand compensation methodologies and processes.\n\n#Instructions\nPlease give a layman's description of the plan component {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ComponentName}} that calculates {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Type}} earnings.\n\nUse the below information to inform your explanation of the plan component.\nEarnings are calculated as {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Type}} using an expression described as {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ExprDescription}}\n\nThe earnings are calculated at the per {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CalcType}} level. When earnings are calculated on a per interval basis this includes total performance over a given period of time. When calculated on a per event basis the earnings are calculated based on results of each individual order or transaction.\n\nPlan components may also include indirect credits in their calculations which means that the payee may receive credit for sales or performance that others produced in addition to their own performance.\n\n\nFor the plan component you're describing\n\nThe component includes {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.CreditType}} indirect credits.\nPayment out frequency is  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Frequency}}\n\n\n##Outline of Response\nAn acceptable response explains how the expression is used to calculate earnings, the level of the calculation (Per Event or Per Interval), the payout frequency, and if indirect credits are applicable.\n\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nProvide a succinct response in a professional tone. Do not provide closing summarizing statement, embellish, or use syntax of the expression in your response. When explaining per interval calculations, do not reference a specific interval. Payout frequency of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Frequency}} is not the same as the calculation interval.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
